      "side": 1,
      "message": "Width here comes from samples[0] only. If samples have different lengths, a longer one produces bits above all_bits, which land in both masks and fail the assert with a misleading “stuck bits” message. Shorter is silently zero-extended.\n\nIf lengths are supposed to be fixed, assert it up front:\n\n   self.assertTrue(all(len(s) \u003d\u003d len(samples[0]) for s in samples))",
      "revId": "d02abe96e14b48a53e4b56e4f970e9c08ec42f50",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
