      "writtenOn": "2026-10-20T04:06:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "“Catches truncated stores” depends on how samples are captured.\n\nIt works if the IV buffer is a fixed size and a short write leaves some bytes zero (or stale). If the truncated output is itself shorter (e.g., the function returns 12 bytes instead of 16), and all samples are short, width shrinks to match and the test passes. Checking len(samples[0]) against the expected IV size would close this gap.",
      "revId": "d02abe96e14b48a53e4b56e4f970e9c08ec42f50",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
